docs/codex-collaboration/README.md:130:2. **DRAIN-FOLDER goal**: every PDF in a named folder ends the session either represented by a `wiki/sources/*.md` page (real ingest), folded into an existing source page (same-DOI rollup), or marked in `data/evidence/wishlist-fetch-audit.csv` with an explicit `skip:*` / `fail:*` / `ingested` decision. Folder ends empty of un-dispositioned PDFs.
docs/codex-collaboration/README.md:144:4. **TRIAGE-FIRST FOR DRAIN-FOLDER GOALS.** Auto-fetched wishlist folders are heavily padded with same-DOI duplicates, false-positives, and download failures. The drain-folder goal is met fastest by: (a) opening every PDF in the folder in parallel batches of 10, (b) classifying each as `real-ingest` / `dedup-rollup` / `skip:<reason>` / `blocker`, (c) batch-committing all `dedup-rollup` and `skip:*` decisions to `wishlist-fetch-audit.csv` in one or two commits, (d) then doing real ingests on the remaining `real-ingest` pile. Interleaving triage with full ingest per PDF is slower.
docs/codex-collaboration/README.md:211:GOAL: <FOLDER_PATH> has 0 un-dispositioned PDFs. Every PDF ends either represented by a wiki/sources/*.md page (real ingest), folded into an existing page as a same-DOI rollup (with the wishlist row marked ingested), or marked in data/evidence/wishlist-fetch-audit.csv with an explicit skip:<reason> or fail:<reason> decision. Stop when met OR hard blocker (paper-internal contradiction, DOI conflict).
docs/codex-collaboration/README.md:213:How: TRIAGE FIRST. Open every PDF in the folder in parallel batches of 10. Classify each as (a) real-ingest, (b) dedup-rollup, (c) skip:<reason>, (d) blocker. Batch-commit all (b)+(c) decisions to wishlist-fetch-audit.csv in one or two commits. Then real-ingest the (a) pile, batch-committing every ~10 source pages. Per CLAUDE.md Part 4, do NOT commit per-paper.
